swmmrs repository licensing
===========================

Copyright 2026 Constantine Karos

Except for the exclusions below, original swmmrs material in this repository is
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The complete license text is in
LICENSES/APACHE-2.0.txt.

This grant includes the public Python and command-line interface source, the
standalone output reader, documentation, scripts, tests, workflows, and other
original public-repository material unless a file states different terms.

Exclusions and separate terms
-----------------------------

1. crates/solver/

   The original swmmrs native solver source is not licensed under the Apache
   License, Version 2.0. No license to that original source is granted except
   through a separate written agreement with the copyright holder. This
   exclusion continues to apply if crates/solver becomes a private git
   submodule.

   This exclusion does not restrict rights that already exist in incorporated
   upstream material. Material created by Open Water Analytics contributors
   remains available under the MIT License, and original USEPA SWMM material is
   identified by the upstream project as public domain. See
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and thirdparty/licenses/OWA-SWMM-MIT.txt.

2. thirdparty/

   Third-party and vendored material is governed by its own license and notice
   files, not by this repository license. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

3. Native release artifacts

   Official wheels and command-line archives may combine Apache-2.0-licensed
   interface code with the separately licensed native solver. Original swmmrs
   binary components are freeware under the swmmrs Binary Runtime License,
   Version 1.0, reproduced in LICENSES/SWMMRS-BINARY-RUNTIME.txt. That license
   permits use, modification, and redistribution of official compiled release
   artifacts for any purpose while granting no access to, or rights in,
   undistributed private solver source. Third-party components remain under
   their own terms.

4. Separately marked files

   A file or directory carrying its own license or copyright notice remains
   governed by those terms.

Nothing in this file grants permission to use project or contributor trademarks
except as allowed by the applicable component license.
